.TH LOG_WRITER.PY 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-downtime-logger 0.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
log_writer.py \- log\-line test producer for the LogfileDetector
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python \-m tools.log_writer
.B \-\-path
.I FILE
.B \-\-message
.I TEXT
.RB [ \-\-count
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-interval
.IR SECS ]
.br
.B python tools/log_writer.py
.I ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Diagnostic tool shipped with
.BR mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger (1).
It creates the parent directory of
.I FILE
if needed and appends
.I N
lines of the form
.PP
.RS
.nf
<ISO\-8601 UTC timestamp> <TEXT>
.fi
.RE
.PP
opening and closing the file for each line.
Choose
.I TEXT
to match one of the detector's
.B down_patterns
or
.BR up_patterns .
.PP
.B The first write to a file that does not yet exist is not seen.
.B LogfileDetector
opens a file it has not got open by seeking to its end, including a file
that appears after the detector started or reappears after a rotation gap.
Lines written before the detector's next poll are therefore skipped.
Run the tool twice, or create
.I FILE
first (for example with
.BR touch (1))
and wait one poll interval.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-path " FILE"
Log file to append to.
Required.
.TP
.BI \-\-message " TEXT"
Text of each line.
Required.
.TP
.BI \-\-count " N"
Number of lines.
Default
.BR 1 .
.TP
.BI \-\-interval " SECS"
Seconds between lines when
.I N
> 1.
Default
.BR 1.0 .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All lines written.
.TP
.B 1
The directory or file cannot be created or written.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error, including a missing
.B \-\-path
or
.BR \-\-message .
.SH EXAMPLES
Drive the
.I local.yaml
log detector DOWN and back UP:
.PP
.RS
.nf
mkdir \-p /tmp/daq\-test; touch /tmp/daq\-test/run.log; sleep 2
python \-m tools.log_writer \-\-path /tmp/daq\-test/run.log \-\-message "RUN STOPPED"
sleep 10
python \-m tools.log_writer \-\-path /tmp/daq\-test/run.log \-\-message "RUN STARTED"
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger (1),
.BR disk_writer.py (1),
.BR mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger.yaml (5)
.SH AUTHOR
Andrew Norman and the Mu2e DAQ group, Fermi National Accelerator Laboratory.
